<title>SPAIN: Spain's SEAT manages output despite French strike.</title>
<headline>Spain's SEAT manages output despite French strike.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volkswagen AG's Spanish unit SEAT SA said it was able to go ahead with normal car production at its Martorell plant on Friday, despite supply problems caused by a French truckers' strike.</p>
<p>&quot;SEAT production will continue because yesterday afternoon we were able to resolve by alternative means the arrival of parts by air transport,&quot; a SEAT spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said normal production of 1,900 vehicles daily should be able to be sustained throughout next week as well.</p>
<p>SEAT had said on Thursday that it was going to have to stop production at Martorell because the truckers' strike was holding up road transport of car parts from Germany.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2151</p>
</text>
